A revert no longer waits after a restart until the startup full scan has
finished (f6cff50, Queue deny and revert until the folder settles), nor while
a scan bracket is open (0289804, Wait for an open scan bracket before deny or
revert): both checks in the revert arm of FolderState::unsettled are removed.
The pin needs both off, as its doc comment says: the simulator starts a
restarted node's full scan at once, so either wait alone still holds a queued
revert until that scan finishes. The deny's open-bracket wait is left as it
is, since this pin's decision is a revert. DESIGN.md §8.3.

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_queued_revert_waits_for_the_startup_scan_to_finish
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_revert_after_a_restart_waits_for_the_startup_scan
